{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For the man is a tree of the field.</b> Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 20:19) explained well, for the proper measure of the verse is: 'for from it you shall eat' — 'for the man is a tree of the field' — 'and it you shall not cut down to come before you in the siege.' And the meaning of 'for the man is a tree of the field' is like 'for he is a living person' (Deuteronomy 24:6). But according to the opinion of our Sages (Bava Kamma 91b), it is permitted to cut down fruit trees to build siege-works, and the Torah said only 'the tree that you know is not a fruit tree,' and so forth, in order to precede and say that a barren tree may be cut before a fruit tree. If so, the meaning of the passage according to them is that the Torah warned 'you shall not destroy its tree' — not to cut them down by way of wanton destruction not for the needs of the siege, as is the custom of armies. And the reason is that those who fight devastate the city and the surrounding land; perhaps they will be able to prevail, as it is said: 'and you shall fell every good tree and stop up every spring of water' (II Kings 3:19). But you shall not do so to destroy it, for you trust in HaShem that He will deliver it into your hand — 'for the man is a tree of the field'; from it you shall eat and live, and through it you shall come against the city before you in siege — to say: you shall live from it after you conquer the city, and also while you are in the camp 'to come before you in the siege' you may do so. And the meaning of 'it you shall destroy and cut down' is that you are permitted to cut it down to build the siege-works and even to destroy it until she falls, for sometimes the destruction is necessary for conquest, for example when the men of the city go out and gather wood from it or hide there in the forest to fight against you, or when it serves the city as a refuge and shelter from plague-stones."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:46.855689711Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}